5fee799f (43 1793047673636 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f352") (src . "store identity survives a remount; a refused write creates nothing\n\nA store's identity binds its directory's device and inode. The device is\nthe kernel's number for the volume, given at mount time, and a reboot\ncan change it while the machine, the inode and the owners stay what they\nwere: after one, every store on the machine refused writes for its\nidentity until it was adopted by hand. The device is now compared last,\nafter the machine, the inode and the owners' nonce, and a device that\nalone differs is a remount, not a copy: a write records it under the\nstore lock it already holds (instance.sexp rewritten with the live\ndevice, the change kept in a remounts history of eight), traced as\n(instance (remounted (from d) (to d'))), and goes on; adopt on such a\nstore answers (reason remount) without deriving or retiring a writer; a\nreplay reaching the barrier without admission records it the same way.\nA copy to another path still has another inode and is refused for it.\ncheck reports the identity and the history in an instance clause.\n\nA write is admitted before it maintains: the identity, the registry\nreservation and the generation are decided first, and only an admitted\nwrite cuts a torn tail or rotates. A write refused for its identity used\nto leave an empty next segment behind, and the adopt that followed named\nthat segment with the previous one's end offset, a point in no segment,\nwhich check read as damage for ever. adopt's prefix now names the last\napplied record's segment; an empty trailing segment is a legal state,\nreported in the writer's check entry.\n\n- log.sc: verify-instance-by compares the device last; remount-held!;\n  admit-write! before maintain-and-write-staged!'s cut and rotation;\n  adopt-decided!'s remount reason and the discovery-end-segment prefix;\n  note-written-for! records a remount; instance-check-clause,\n  trailing-empty-segment.\n- store.sc: check's instance clause and the writer's empty-segment\n  reading.\n- README: remount, the limit (a volume clone keeping inode numbers is\n  taken for a remount; cp -R and adopt separates it), check and adopt.\n- Tests: adopt1 (the remount, the refusals, the empty-segment shape, the prefix\n  shapes), daemon-e1 (remount under a daemon), append-prefix, log13 and\n  q7 (rows that pinned the old order, rewritten), rows-baseline,\n  change-stream-guard-expect (the intended check change).\n") (parent . root) (ord . 483))))
